            "type": "text",
            "value": " values onto the end of a vector (which will grow the vector as needed):"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "code_block",
        "language": null,
        "code": "let mut v = vec![1, 2];\n\nv.push(3);"
      },
      {
        "type": "link",
        "href": "https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0Afn+main()+%7B%0A++++let+mut+v+=+vec!%5B1,+2%5D;%0A++++%0A++++v.push(3);%0A%7D&edition=2024",
        "title": "Run code",
        "children": []
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Popping values works in much the same way:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "code_block",
        "language": null,
        "code": "let mut v = vec![1, 2];\n\nlet two = v.pop();"
      },
